The cost for the second 8 glasses is:
\[ 8 \times 3 = 24 \text{ dollars} \]

Adding these costs together gives the total cost for 16 glasses:
\[ 40 + 24 = 64 \text{ dollars} \]

Therefore, Kylar needs to pay $64 for 16 glasses.

